A||||6||Gold87SE||More problems||||1||
Z||000000||Gold87SE||02-23-2001||10:27 PM||||I recently posted how my car sort of jerks back and forth going down hills. Well, today I noticed that when I spin the tires in the snow(even slightly), the car hops rather violently. It's not the tires hopping, it's in the motor or trans. Could this be a transmission problem?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||02-23-2001||11:04 PM||||Check ALL your mounts 4 the engine and trans.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold87SE||02-23-2001||11:52 PM||||I'll have them checked out tomorrow. I do notice that the engine feels kind of unstable, especially when going up hills. The car also jerks pretty hard when I put it in drive or reverse. Thanks for your help.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||02-25-2001||12:44 PM||||check the upper engine strut (dogbone) -- that is usually the first mount that will deteriorate......also, on yours there is a lower strut (kinda like a little shock absorber) as well as the motor and tranny mounts on the cradle.......personally, from my experiences here at the shop, the ones I have seen which acted like you are describing had very bad dogbones.......in addition to the dogbone itself, make sure that the holes in the mounting brackets for the dogbone are not enlongated from wear.......||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gold87SE||03-06-2001||03:34 PM||||I just found out that it's a torque converter lock-up solenoid problem. I disconnected four pin connector from the transmission and the problem went away. Does anybody have any idea around how much this could cost to fix?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||03-06-2001||03:47 PM||||The part is under $30 and then a coupla qts. of fluid and you're set.(doing it yourself of course)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||03-06-2001||05:41 PM||||You'll also need the side cover gasket.  You might as well change the filter and all the fluid while you are at it.||||reg||1
